  cost 1   min(a, b)                                the select a < b ? a : b as min(a, b) (derived)
      holds where neither compared value is NaN (GLSL leaves min and max undefined there; the select takes the second arm), and where they are zeros of opposite signs the zero's sign may differ (both allowed by Vulkan's default float controls, without SignedZeroInfNanPreserve)
      the select takes a exactly where b is above it (a < b), and b otherwise; where they are equal both arms are the same value; floats other than NaN are ordered (with -0 = +0), so that is min(a, b) wherever no operand is NaN, up to the sign of a zero
